# Parallel agents all append their entry at the same anchor in the changelog, so every
# concurrent branch collides there and the resolution is always the same one: keep both
# entries. `union` is git's built-in driver for exactly that, and it costs a session the
# hand-resolution each time it is missing — four of them in one round of six branches.
#
# It is right here because entries are appended whole and independently. A merge where two
# sides genuinely rewrite the *same* paragraph will keep both versions rather than conflict,
# which is visible in review; nothing else in the tree gets this treatment for that reason.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
